-- ============================================================
-- Black Alibi MM2 | stable release
-- version : 1.0.2
-- author  : by GachiRave
-- target  : Murder Mystery 2
--
-- how roles are read (no waiting for the 10s role selector):
--   1. GetPlayerData, requested once when the script starts
--   2. Fade / UpdatePlayerData events sent by MM2
--   3. equipment, only as a silent fallback
-- hero is layered on top: the round's sheriff is remembered from the
-- data, and any other player holding the gun afterwards is painted Hero
--
-- ============================================================
-- CHANGELOG 1.0.2
-- ============================================================
-- ADDED
--   Auto Server Hop. If the round assigns you anything other than
--   Murderer, the script waits a beat and hops you into a new server.
--
--   Throw Knife Hotkey. A draggable button appears in a screen corner.
--   Tapping it throws the knife at the best target: a visible Sheriff
--   inside range always wins, otherwise the closest visible player is
--   used. The same line of sight check as the aimbot blocks wall hits.
--
--   Coin ESP, Auto Fire On Lock for the Sheriff/Hero side, and Fall
--   Recovery, which pulls you back onto solid ground before you drop
--   into the void.
--
--   Check My Role button on the ESP tab. Re-reads the round data and
--   slides a banner in from the top of the screen for four seconds,
--   even before the in-game role reveal UI shows up.
--
-- FIXED
--   Kill All could crash the client outright. A ragdolled or glitched
--   body can carry a NaN or wildly out of range CFrame, and handing
--   that straight to PivotTo was the real cause, not the player count.
--   Every position is now checked for sane, finite numbers before any
--   teleport, the whole sweep runs inside pcall, and the running flag
--   always clears, even after an error.
--
--   Kill All now stops immediately if the murderer dies or drops the
--   knife mid sweep, instead of continuing to swing at nothing.
--
-- CHANGED
--   Prediction Aimbot uses an adaptive response curve: a fast, decisive
--   snap up close and a gentler approach at range, instead of one fixed
--   smoothing value that overshot on long sightlines.
--
--   Window enlarged to fit the new tools without crowding the layout.
--   Toggle rows and panel toggles now give a short press animation.
-- ============================================================
-- CHANGELOG 1.0.1
-- ============================================================
-- ADDED
--   Prediction Aimbot tracks the murderer's body and calculates horizontal
--   lead from distance, network latency and smoothed assembly velocity.
--   Vertical lead is handled separately and capped to one stud, so a jumping
--   target cannot drag the crosshair several metres into the air.
--
--   Kill All in the murderer panel. One sweep over every living player
--   instead of waiting for them to walk into aura range.
--
--   Auto Grab Gun on the Extra tab. Watches for the drop and collects it
--   automatically, then returns you to the spot you were standing on.
--
-- FIXED
--   Kill Aura range was never written into a config. Saving a preset kept
--   the toggles but the slider always came back as 12. The number is part
--   of the snapshot now and is restored on load.
--
--   Line of sight could still approve a target behind thin or one sided
--   geometry, so the aim sometimes locked through a wall. The check now
--   samples the head, torso and lower body, and any solid hit blocks it.
--
-- CHANGED
--   Renamed from Black Alibi GachiRave to Black Alibi MM2.
--   Page transitions, toggle feedback and notification motion reworked.
-- ============================================================

